    -- legacy 01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91 (done): Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol
    -- The Zenoh service client adapter exists and nothing answers it. The service side of the protocol
    -- must take a holder's request, ask the service core, and return the completion the client checks.
    -- This item plans that server half as plain Rust in the component library, so a host test can drive
    -- it. It adds the exam that grades the server half against bytes the judge writes itself. The exam
    -- fails until the implementation lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1d30356c73"
      "Each completion the server returns equals the bytes that `struct` writes from `completionLayout`. Each sample header in the data page equals the bytes written from `sampleHeaderLayout`. The server stamps the timestamp from the time it is given."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1e50236979"
      "A publication on a key reaches every holder with a subscribe row on it, the publisher included. A holder with no publish row on the key is denied, and so is a holder with no rows. A refused publication reaches no ring. A holder that attaches twice is denied."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1fe3015eed"
      "A full ring drops its oldest sample and says so once, before the samples that remain. A take into a buffer smaller than the next sample is refused and the sample stays. After a detach or an abort the holder has no session."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab208d112e7b"
      "No completion the exam lists is one the client refuses. A failure carries its status and nothing else. A request outside the protocol is answered with the operation it names and changes nothing."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab21afa0707a"
      "The exam refuses 104 inputs. Eighty-five remove or change one line of the transcript. Fifteen break a rule the client applies to a completion, and that includes a publish refusal that does not echo its row. Four corrupt the schema's layout, and the honest transcript must then be refused."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 104; } "The checker refuses exactly 104 inputs. Each one changes the transcript, the client's rules or the layout, and the judge must refuse it. The unaltered transcript is accepted first.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab2220b92f5d"
      "`just zenoh_service_server_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_server_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run needs the Rust test.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a19c28-fbe6-72f4-ae88-b6d4f0d9b2e4 (done): Plan the Zenoh service component crate and its registration
