        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_component_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 16; } "The checker refuses exactly 16 file sets. Each declaration is removed in turn from a synthetic file set, and the refusal must name it. The unaltered set is accepted first.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-fbe6-72f4-ae88-b6d4f0d9b2e4"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae43-72dc-95af-58f9f04b8002"
      "`just zenoh_service_component_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh service component crate and its registration"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_component_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run reads the crate.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-fbe6-72f4-ae88-b6d4f0d9b2e4"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40 (done): Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange
    -- No composition runs the Zenoh service, and the demo nodes each run their own session. This item
    -- plans the composition `sel4-zenoh-service`. It holds the service, its holders and the grants between
    -- them, derived from a system spec. The arm that boots it under QEMU and its judge land in this
    -- planning change. The exam fails until the composition lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b462d73b4ad"
      "A system spec `sel4-zenoh-service` declares an instance `zenoh-service` with its executable, a network application row for it, a grants list and the grants object. The manifest derived from it holds the same. One entry of the composition inventory names the composition and the owning gate `zenoh_service_booted_check`, and a test-run record names its closure."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_booted_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 19; } "The checker counts 19 cases. 18 are declarations that the files must hold, and one is the booted run. The count is exact. Only the booted run shows the holders exchanging through the service.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b473b2bf634"
      "`RELEASE_INPUTS` lists `scripts/lib/zenoh_grants_table.py` and the directory `contracts/zenoh-service-grants-table/v1`. An edit to either changes a closure identity, so a generation that carries grants cannot change without its closure changing."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_booted_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 19; } "The checker counts 19 cases. 18 are declarations that the files must hold, and one is the booted run. The count is exact. Only the booted run shows the holders exchanging through the service.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b4852f0e576"
      "`check-sel4-io-network-plane.py` offers the arm `zenoh-service` and imports the judge `zenoh_service_arm`. The marker chains require a holder to attach and the holders to exchange samples. They require a denial of class `not-granted` with `refused=1` for a key a holder lacks. The judge requires every publication to reach as many holders as it says."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_booted_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 19; } "The checker counts 19 cases. 18 are declarations that the files must hold, and one is the booted run. The count is exact. Only the booted run shows the holders exchanging through the service.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b4935c6f2e6"
      "The arm boots the image of the composition under QEMU, and its marker chains match in order with no failure marker. The test-run record bounds the run by a timeout."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_booted_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 19; } "The checker counts 19 cases. 18 are declarations that the files must hold, and one is the booted run. The count is exact. Only the booted run shows the holders exchanging through the service.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b4adfe35cab"
      "The exam refuses 63 inputs. 18 remove one declaration from a synthetic file set, and the refusal must name it. The other 45 mutate an honest transcript of the service. The judge must refuse each."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_booted_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 63; } "The checker refuses exactly 63 inputs. Each declaration is removed in turn from a synthetic file set, and the refusal must name it. The honest transcript is accepted first, and then each mutation of it is refused. The marker chains are held to the shared controls of the gate checker, which the pin of 261 markers covers.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae50-71fd-a429-4b4be578466d"
      "`just zenoh_service_booted_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh service composition and its booted exchange"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_booted_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges and someone runs it under QEMU.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c29-056e-79a2-81a5-7d833c275b40"; }; };
  }) with {
    nonGoals = {
      "The component that wraps the core, the client interface, the path of the grants from the system spec to the service, and a booted composition. A later item owns them, and it cannot be graded until this one lands.";
      "A holder that names a topic and a type. Lazy declaration on the first subscribe. Reliable delivery with credits. A per-row option to exclude a holder's own publications. The decision record lists each as not taken.";
      "More than one peer, discovery, queryables, wildcard keys, and anything that the Profile 0 decoder refuses today.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The core, the event change and the Rust test module belong to the implementation.";
      "The client protocol and the client library in `components/lib`. The path of the grants from the system spec to the service. The component and a booted composition. Later items own them.";
      "Removing or changing the session-based core and its exam. They stay as merged.";
      "An acknowledgement from the peer. Profile 0 has none, so the core can know that the link took the bytes and no more.";
      "A bound on the notice queue other than the one the exam observes. The exam observes eight notices and records what a burst does to them.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The Rust modules and the link change belong to the implementation.";
      "A check that the implementation's test drives the server. The test prints the transcript, and the judge reads what it prints. A test that printed the 39 expected lines without calling the server would pass. The implementation pull request is reviewed for that, and a checker-owned harness would close it.";
      "The server half. It is a module in `components/lib` that the implementation pull request adds with the component and the reader.";
      "The IO0 ring and the loans. The component owns them. The server half takes request bytes and returns completion bytes and the data page.";
      "The clock. The server half takes the time as an argument, and the exam advances it by one for each publication.";
      "What the component does when a holder faults or never detaches. The exam grades detach and abort as the protocol states them.";
      "A holder with more than two rows or a ring with more than two slots. The exam uses two holders with rows, one holder without, and a ring of two samples.";
      "The crate. The implementation pull request adds it with the server half and the grants reader.";
      "The holders' endpoints, the composition and the booted run. The composition item owns them.";
      "The stack size and the memory of the core and the link at real sizes. Nobody has computed them. The implementation states them in the component spec, and the exam does not check the values.";
      "The component's reaction to a holder that faults. The exam shows that the crate exists and does not show what its loop does.";
      "The composition and the generated outputs. The implementation pull request adds them.";
      "A boot of the arm. No image exists for it, and the marker chains have never matched a real transcript. The implementation pull request is the first to boot it and may need to tune the chains in a separate planning change.";
      "The choice of holders. The exam requires the service instance, the grants object and the arm's markers. It does not name the holders.";
      "A stock peer or an external network. The composition uses the network service's loopback backend.";
      "A CI job for the booted run. The owner decides that after the run has a measured duration.";
      "The closure sources. The implementation pull request adds the two closure inputs and regenerates every closure source in a derived commit, because it changes the closure input set.";
    };
  };

area
